hey everyone its Johanna here are you a  late-night snack err do you stay up late  nights because your work demands it or  perhaps you are a student preparing for  an upcoming examination or it's a TV  show keeping you up well whatever your  reasons are late night snacking mainly  to regain and it can also sabotage your  weight loss effort  hence choosing the right snack is key to  satisfy your cravings or hunger without  packing on the high amount of calories  which mainly feel feeling bloated and  regretful in the morning so if you are a  late night snack err I want you to stick  to these three rules first your snacks  should be under 200 calories remember  this is a snack not a meal if you over  it especially late at night when we are  physically inactive those calories are  more likely to be stored as fat second  drink a glass of water first and wait  for at least 20 minutes before you start  stacking this will allow your brain to  register whether are you truly hungry or  are you just dehydrated  or bored third if you feel the urge to  snack out of boredom then ask yourself  why am I still up so late at night  shouldn't I be in bed lack of sleep can  also sabotage your weight loss effort so  to help you with your snacking here are  my top 10 healthy and nutritious  late-night snacks which are also under  100 calories my number one choice has to  be my favorite frozen yogurt ice cream  instead of the typical creamy high  calories high fat ice cream this  healthier alternative is light low in  calories and satisfied my ice cream  cravings to make them I've used 50 gram  of sliced bananas 150 gram of frozen  strawberries or any other fruits of your  choice 200 gram of Greek although fat  plain yogurt and 1 tbsp of goji berries  blend all the ingredients until thick  and smooth  then place the mixture into six popsicle  mos freeze them overnight and you can  enjoy your guilt free ice cream  throughout the week and the best part is  each stick is only 40 calories so in  fact you can treat yourself to two  sticks this second stack is perfect for  a late night movie pop cards are  generally low in calories recording at  only 31 calories per cup this is of  course the no butter no sugar plain  popcorns so instead of buying ready  popcorns which are loaded with fat and  added sugar let's go back to the basic  and make our own healthy popcorns and  add our own flavors it is really simple  place cut a cup of popcorn kernels into  a microwave-safe bowl cover firmly  either with a lid or a plate you want to  make sure that there is no gap between  the bowl and plate microwave it for  about 5 minutes or until the popping  slows down be careful when removing from  the microwave as the dish is very hot  finally top it up with your own flavors  I've coated mine with honey allow them  to cool down and you have your healthy  movie snack ready to munch aged 2 cups  of serving with 1/2 a tbsp of honey is  only 94 calories stall the rest away in  a food container and you will always  have your healthy movie snacks for  emergency if you are truly hungry and  you want a bigger portion without adding  the extra amount of calories then a bowl  of warm soup is perfect at this time of  the night  avoid creamy ones and go for broth-based  soup which is lighter and easier to  digest and of course skip the noodles  and starchy cups to avoid bloating and  the extra calories which may be stored  as fat I've made my seafood vegetable  soup with 2 cups of vegetable broth 50  gram of green leafy vegetables and  carrots 1 ounce or 30 gram of prawns and  1 tbsp of goji berries this bowl which  looks like  Mill only has 93 calories so if you want  your Chinese takeaway make your own  vegetable soup instead we all know that  vegetables are healthy low in calories  keep you satisfied and perfect to be  eaten all day long so my next favorite  late-night snack is carrots and hummus  instead of buying the dips I have made  my own hummus the ingredients you'll  need are half a can of chickpeas washed  and drained cut a cup of Greek or plain  yogurt 1 clove of garlic minced half a  teaspoon of olive oil quarter teaspoon  of dried parsley and quantity spoon of  paprika place all the ingredients in to  food processor and process until you  have a smooth and creamy texture my  carrots and hummus is under 100 calories  you can always change the vegetables and  dips to your own taste if you are  working or studying late-night and you  need something to munch on to keep you  going try this out you can always make a  few containers store them in the fridge  and when you have the urge to munch you  have a healthy snack to turn to my next  quick easy and healthy snack to go for  is tuna sandwich crackers instead of  choosing bread which is more dense and  has more calories go for whole grain or  whole wheat crackers instead which  typically has about 35 calories each -  whole grain crackers spread with quater  can of tuna only has 100 calories this  is light high in protein and high in  complex carbs which can help to control  further cravings  most of us start our day with a bowl of  cereal or oatmeal and this can actually  be part of your healthy late night snack  I tend to have this myself as well at  times what you want to avoid is the  sugary cereals so go for smaller portion  go for a small bowl of whole grain or  whole wheat cereals to curb hunger for  instance one pane Weetabix with quarter  cup of semi skimmed milk only has ninety  eight point two five calories so you can  have your breakfast as your late-night  snack  if for some reason you crave muffins  cakes or banana why not try my zucchini  bread and banana muffin recipes instead  remember that all my recipes are  interchangeable so you can have them for  breakfast as your afternoon snack or  even late night snack more healthy and  light snacks perfect for the nighttime  include yogurt and fruits 100 gram of  low-fat yogurt with 1 TSP of raw honey  and quarter cup of strawberries only has  100 calories  hot chocolate my favorite you have seen  me drink this prior to bedtime a warm  glass of milk or hot chocolate will not  only help you sleep better it can also  reduce food cravings one cup of  unsweetened soy milk with one teaspoon  of cocoa powder only has about a 98  calories and of course you can choose to  sweeten it with honey or stevia I love  this other healthy late night snack  ideas include whole fruit nuts dry  fruits  healthy snack bar and even an egg what  you want to avoid is obviously takeaways  high-fat greasy food  caffeine energy drink alcohol and  starchy food which tends to be high in  calories in fact even all the healthy  foods should be consumed in moderation  to avoid slip in digestion bloating and  excess calories intake tackling late  night snacking and cravings is also  about being prepared the more healthy  snacks you have in a fridge the more  likely you are to reach for them instead  opting for the unhealthy options so the  more prepared you are the more likely  you will stick to your fitness goal the  question is are you a late-night snack  err for new fitness food and  motivational videos please like share  and subscribe to my youtube channel and  website do you follow me on Facebook  Instagram and Twitter to stay connected  with me thanks guys  you
 

